---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section class="sec" id="needs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rv">
      <div class="label">Know which one needs you</div>
      <h2 class="h2">Stop watching terminals.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        Anything waiting on you is turquoise, and nothing else is. One strip above the board lists it for the
        open project. Other projects show a badge on the rail, and ⌘J moves on to them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ny">
      <div class="nyc rv">
        <div class="vis">
          <div style="width:100%">
            <div
              class="strip"
              style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--st-attn-bg)"
            >
              <span class="t">Needs you · 3</span>
              <span class="ch on">
                <span class="k">SHOP-22</span>allow a command
              </span>
              <span class="ch on">
                <span class="k">SHOP-12</span>a question
              </span>
              <span class="ch on">
                <span class="k">SHOP-32</span>decide
              </span>
              <span class="nx">
                Next <span class="kbd">⌘J</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tx">
          <h3>The Needs you strip</h3>
          <p>
            One chip per thing waiting on you: a permission prompt, a question, your check, a check that
            failed three times. An open question stays until it’s answered, even when you answer in the
            terminal.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nyc rv">
        <div class="vis">
          <div class="notif">
            <span class="dotp" style="margin-top:4px"></span>
            <div>
              <div class="ti">SHOP-12 asks you</div>
              <div class="bd">Follow the system setting for dark mode? · shop-web</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tx">
          <h3>A notification, when it matters</h3>
          <p>
            Permission prompts, questions and stopped agents send a macOS notification. None while that
            ticket’s terminal has focus. Working normally is quiet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nyc rv">
        <div class="vis">
          <div class="pausem">
            <div class="h">
              <Icon icon="pause" />
              Pause
            </div>
            <div class="i on">
              This project
              <span class="kbd" style="margin-left:auto">
                ⇧⌘.
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="i">All projects</div>
            <div class="n">Stops spending at once. Survives restarts. Never lifts on its own.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tx">
          <h3>Pause, and it stays paused</h3>
          <p>
            One button holds every agent in a project, or all of them. Nothing is lost, and nothing resumes
            until you say so.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
